# Python runtime float arguments

Each case supplies the same Auto source to the ordinary AV run and the A2PY run-py check. The independent Python reference and the interpreter setup live in the python-1129 fixture directory.

## Case: runtime-values
id: "py.float-args.1129.runtime-values"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1129"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.as"
syntax: "auto-script"

```auto
use.py struct: pack

fn scale(x float, k float) float {
    return x * k
}

fn main() int {
    var step = 3
    var rate = 0.05f + step.as(float) * 0.01f
    print(pack(">f", rate).hex().to(str))
    var lr = 0.1d * 3.0d
    print(pack(">d", lr).hex().to(str))
    print(pack(">f", scale(1.0f, 0.1f)).hex().to(str))
    var again = 0.25
    again = 0.5
    print(pack(">f", again).hex().to(str))
    print(pack(">f", 0.1).hex().to(str))
    print(pack(">d", 0.1d).hex().to(str))
    print(pack(">d", -0.0d).hex().to(str))
    print(pack(">f", -0.0f).hex().to(str))
    print(pack(">d", 0.0d).hex().to(str))
    return 0
}
```

